Five months and few buckets of sweat later, I can report that Matt Ftzgerald's advice on 80 20 runnong works for me!
It brought me 40 mins improvement of PB in marathon, from 5h to 4:23-but even better than just the time difference was the fashion in which I finished: with a sprint!
Now, sure, I might just had a good day, but I need to add that I made about 80% of MFitzgerald's plan, never got injured and improved most of my recent PB's.
And... I learned a pile! About my heart rates and pace and whatever on what Garmin watch can inform me. I feel that in the next season I might go for the next notch
better, just running more carefully inside the zones. Now I was actually quite lacking on rigor on this, or simply ability to do it slowly...but I did my best! And
already this helped. Let's see if with a bit more work in the next season I can go below 4hrs. Without injury, that is, and without burnout!
